Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:50:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Leave the Ethernet switch out on the W541

On a ThinkPad W541 the switch turned the GbE off, but turning it back
on did not bring the controller back: with BUC bit 5 cleared and a CF9
0x0E reset, the sequence of the Lenovo firmware with its HECI hidden,
then warm reboots and a power-down with the AC adapter and the battery
out, 00:19.0 stays absent, while every PCH register that can be read
matches a boot where it was present and the descriptor, GbE and ME
regions of the flash are unchanged. The disabled state is kept
somewhere else, likely by the ME in the RTC well, which only a removal
of the coin cell clears.

Do not select SOUTHBRIDGE_INTEL_LYNXPOINT_GBE_OPTION on the W541 until
the way back is known: romstage leaves BUC alone, and the option is
not in the menu. A value saved by a build with the option is ignored.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init; the menu
without "Ethernet".

Change-Id: I80bc8bd9756101eb4d826f170b29cddf0fc4686e
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Kconfig | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Kconfig
index 08cd64055e..84d9407686 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Kconfig
@@ -40,7 +40,6 @@ config BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_T440P
 
 config BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541
 	select BOARD_LENOVO_HASWELL_COMMON
-	select SOUTHBRIDGE_INTEL_LYNXPOINT_GBE_OPTION
 
 if BOARD_LENOVO_HASWELL_COMMON
 
